# Kavacha patch 0053 — extension recommendations in workspace templates
# (REMAINING_WORK.md §3: "deferred at 0006 until the marketplace could install
# them; the marketplace now exists").
#
# THE PREMISE WAS WRONG, and saying so is most of this patch. The marketplace
# (0028, ADR 0010) installs Kavacha COMPONENTS — themes, layouts, bundles —
# not WebExtensions. It was never going to be the installer for uBlock Origin,
# and waiting for it to become one would have deferred this forever. The right
# installer already ships and is Firefox's own.
#
# WHAT: each template carries a short `recommendedExtensions` list, and a panel
# offers it once the Space exists. Nothing is installed automatically, silently,
# or as a side effect of creating a Space: "Get extension" opens the
# addons.mozilla.org LISTING in a tab — not an .xpi — so the user sees the
# permissions, reviews and source, and the install runs through AMO's and
# Firefox's own prompts. Already-installed recommendations show as such rather
# than as a button that would do nothing.
#
# One composite action is offered: "Run only these in this Space" writes patch
# 0004's per-Space allowlist from the recommendations that are actually
# installed. It is disabled until at least one is, because an allowlist of
# nothing would silently disable every extension in that Space.
#
# EDITORIAL NOTE: recommending an extension is an endorsement, and this is the
# first place Kavacha makes one. The list is deliberately short and everything
# on it is open-source, widely audited, and consistent with what Kavacha
# already does by default. It is a product decision as much as a technical one
# and should be reviewed as such — the mechanism is the durable part.
#
# The command is available only where a Space actually has recommendations, so
# it does not sit dead in the palette for hand-made Spaces (workspace.template
# was already stored by 0006, so no new field is needed).
#
# Why a patch: the template table and the panel handler are both inside
# nsZenWorkspaces, and the panel itself lives in Zen's popupset.
#
# Touches: src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceManager.mjs (table + panel + allowlist),
#          src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc (panel),
#          src/zen/common/sys/KavachaCommandRegistry.sys.mjs (palette command),
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl,
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl.
# Applies on top of 0052.
diff --git a/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl b/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl
--- a/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl
+++ b/locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl
@@ -217,3 +217,15 @@
     .label = Preview
